    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSeafront home with permission to expand\n\nSet on a generous 0.47 acre / 0.19 hectare site directly on Strand Road in Annagassan, this three-bedroom bungalow occupies one of the more quietly coveted positions in the very popular area. The sea is not merely a backdrop here — it is a constant presence, with full open-water views from the property and direct access to the beach just steps away. Whether you are drawn by the prospect of morning sea swims, long walks along the shoreline, or simply the pace of life that comes with a coastal village, this is a home that delivers on all of those things without compromise.\n\nExtending to 850 sq ft / 79 sq m, the accommodation is well considered and easy to manage — an important quality for those looking to simplify without sacrificing comfort or setting. The layout flows from an entrance hall into a bright living room and a kitchen and dining room, all orientated to make the most of the outlook. Three bedrooms are served by both a shower room and a separate bathroom, providing day-to-day practicality. The current owners have received full planning permission to extend and modernise the home and further details can provided by the agent upon request. \n\nThe wider setting brings its own appeal. The Cooley Mountains and Mourne range frame the horizon to the north and east, adding a layer of drama to views that already take in open water. Salterstown Pier, a popular spot for sea swimming and walking, is close at hand, and the unhurried rhythm of village life in Annagassan — good coffee, a proper restaurant, familiar faces — is something that is genuinely difficult to replicate elsewhere. For those who have spent years in busier surroundings, this is the kind of place that tends to feel immediately right."
      },
      {
